  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the phrase \"$8$ is even and it is an even number\" to just \"$8$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$8$ is even, and $8$ is even and it is a positive number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$8$ is even and $8$ is even, and it is a positive number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$8$ is even and $8$ is even\" to just \"$8$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$8$ is even, and it is a positive number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$8$ is even and positive.\"",
